A||N||11||Bugsy||Noisy ECM??||||5||
Z||000000||Bugsy||11-26-2001||05:30 AM||||The last few weeks I've noticed a clicking sound coming from the ECM.  Is this something I should be worrying about?  Is the computer dying?  Am I worrying for nothing? Any input is greatly appreciated<BR><P>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin||||reg||5
Z||000001||dennis_6||11-26-2001||07:27 AM||||Sounds like a relay to me.  That should be nothing to worry about.  A relay is an electro-mechanical switch that sometimes makes noise.<p>[This message has been edited by dennis_6 (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||11-26-2001||08:53 AM||||Are you sure it's coming from the ECM?<BR>AFAIK, there are no moving parts inside it. Any relays should be external, and will be controlled by solid state devices within the ECM. <BR>There are two relays on the firewall, directly behind the driver. One is for the fuel pump and the other is for the AC. Maybe you're hearing them?<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||dennis_6||11-26-2001||12:58 PM||||Maybe I am mistaken, but I have heard there are small pc board mounted relays in the ECM.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-26-2001||07:21 PM||||There are no moving parts of any kind in stock GM ECMs used in Fiero. No relays.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroPerformance||11-26-2001||07:32 PM||||I hear the same thing sometimes. It has been doing it off and on for about a year with no problems. I don't think you have anything to worry about. I am 99% sure it is coming from the ECM. It is more a an electirc chatter than a mechanical tick. It doesn't sound loud enough to be a relay.<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||dennis_6||11-27-2001||01:44 AM||||I stand corrected.  I wasn't for sure.  Just posting what I have been told.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bugsy||11-28-2001||02:52 AM||||Thanx guys for setting my mind @ ease, I can't afford another expense at the present time.  I just finished installing a heater core, and now the blower won't work, in addition i just bought a clutch master and slave that i have to install, not to mention another computer crash <P>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin||||reg||14
Z||000008||FieroPerformance||11-28-2001||02:50 PM||||Now that I think about it, the sound could be a lifter tapping. I am not sure.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Patrick86GT||11-28-2001||10:15 PM||||Hey guys...don't overlook the "piece of crap" fuel pump the cheap managers @ GM put into the tank under the console.....||||reg||1
Z||000010||Mach10||11-29-2001||03:23 AM||||OR... The fire-wall grommet-thingies that the ECM wires fee through may be loose... ||||reg||10
Z||000011||Bugsy||12-04-2001||12:43 PM||||I didn't hear the noise till I had to gut the interior to replace the shifter....when uncovered I could hear the ecm chattering. now that its covered again, I can't hear it at all.  The fuel pump?....never had a problem with mine...altho it does make a humming sound when you deprive it of fuel....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin||||reg||10
